WHY A COMMERCIAL LICENSE IS OFFERED

Section 6 of the LGPL requires that whoever receives your application be able
to relink it against a modified version of this library. For an application
that links the library statically and is distributed through an app store,
meeting that requirement is difficult in practice — the recipient generally has
no way to relink the binary the store delivered to them.

The commercial license exists for those who cannot meet the LGPL's terms. It
removes the relinking obligation. It is an alternative to the LGPL, not a
restriction on it: nothing here narrows the rights the LGPL grants you, and if
the LGPL suits your project, you need nothing from Druware.

To obtain a commercial license, contact:

    support@druware.com


